course: dictionary
lesson: 7345
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A plateau is a large, flat area of high land, higher than the land around it. «Yaks live on the Tibetan plateau, often above 4000 metres.» The clues are high and flat, so a plateau must be a high, level place.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Yaks live on the high, flat land of the Tibetan plateau» still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
explain: Plateau can also mean a time when something stops going up or down. «Her progress reached a plateau.» Progress is how far you have got, so a plateau here means progress has stopped rising and stays level. To plateau is to stop growing or improving and stay level.
explain: The same word can mean different things in different subjects. On a line graph, a plateau is the flat part where the value stays the same. Always read the clues around the word to find out which meaning is right.
fact: A plateau is a landform, like a mountain or a valley.
fact: The Tibetan plateau is a very high, flat area where yaks live.
fact: On a line graph, a plateau is the flat part where the value stays the same.
fact: In sport and learning, you «hit a plateau» when you stop improving for a while.
fact: Plateau is a noun (plural plateaus or plateaux) and a verb (plateau, plateaued, plateauing).
exercise: «Yaks live on the Tibetan plateau, often above 4000 metres.» What is a plateau here? | A small pond in a forest | A fast-moving river | A deep valley between two rivers | *A large, flat area of high land
exercise: «Her progress reached a plateau.» What does plateau mean here? | A type of bread | *A time when progress stops going up and stays level | A dark cave | A big jump forward
exercise: Tom says the flat part of his line graph is a plateau. What does the flat part show? | The value falls to zero | Erupt | The value goes up fast | *The value stays the same
test: Ella says she has hit a plateau in piano. What does she mean? | She has finished all her music | She has climbed to the top of a mountain | She has started a new lesson | *She has stopped improving for a while
test: Which word means to stop growing and stay level? | Erupt | Spin | Shout | *Plateau
exam: Which sentence uses plateau to mean a large, flat area of high land? | Her plateau reached the top of the page | *Yaks graze on the high plateau above the valley | The kettle was on the plateau | The plateau was a loud, sudden noise
